  "verbalization": "Neomycin is linked to VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions involving hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that neomycin acts as a target for hepatocytes, which in turn are targets of specific compounds, including (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one and (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one. These compounds are all implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, indicating a potential pathway where neomycin indirectly influences VMRC-LCP through its interaction with hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that neomycin may act as a modulator of the downstream targets, possibly by affecting the cellular environment or signaling pathways that lead to VMRC-LCP activation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of hepatocytes as a critical intermediary in the relationship between neomycin and VMRC-LCP.",
